  "id": "mirror-reading",
  "term": "mirror reading",
  "definition": "Mirror reading is a non-motor procedural learning task or skill in which a person learns to read mirror-inverted words through practice. It is used to study how people acquire and retain cognitive procedural learning, including both general mirror-reading skill and learning for specific repeated words.",
